; Explain why the second noun phrase gave no single object
;
; Reached from #R$7DBC when the first noun phrase is settled (one object) and
; the second is not. RecWork1 ($793E) says what
; the matcher saw of the second phrase: bit 0 the player typed words for it,
; bit 1 some object or place fitted them; $7941 (RecWork3+1) counts the
; candidates the command accepted. The cases:
; .
; 1. No words typed, a second noun is needed: #R$7E4D asks "... what ?" or says
; there is nothing to use.
; .
; 2. Words typed, nothing fitted them: #R$7DFE looks for a place or any object of
; that name, and else says "I do not see ... here".
; .
; 3. Fitting candidates, none accepted: #R$7DF5 runs the command in perform mode so
; that its own refusal is printed.
; .
; 4. Several accepted (the player must choose): the record is saved and "Which
; ... ?" is asked (#R$7D89). This case is odd: the code loads A twice and puts
; the address RecBuf2 ($7948) on the stack where #R$7D83 puts the first word of
; the phrase, so the question prints a stray word ("Which ting ?") and
; AwaitingAnswer gets the low byte of that word instead of the offset of the
; phrase. Not executed with the inputs in re/maps; seen by calling this
; routine with RecWork1 = 3 and $7941 = 2.
; .
; Like #R$7DBC it ends by returning to the caller of #R$79B6 or jumping to the
; end of the turn code at #R$798E.
@label=ExplainNoun2Failure
c$7D98 LD HL,$793E   ; RecWork1
 $7D9B BIT 0,(HL)    ; words typed for phrase 2?
 $7D9D JP Z,$7E4D    ; ReportNoSecondNoun
 $7DA0 BIT 1,(HL)    ; a candidate fitted?
 $7DA2 LD HL,$7948   ; RecBuf2
 $7DA5 LD DE,$B6E9   ; SecondObject
 $7DA8 LD BC,$B6FF   ; Noun2Kind
 $7DAB JR Z,$7DFE    ; FindNounElsewhere
@isub=LD A,(RecWork3+1)
 $7DAD LD A,($7941)  ; candidates accepted
 $7DB0 AND A         ;
 $7DB1 JP Z,$7DF5    ; none: PerformRefusal
@isub=LD A,(RecWork6+1)
 $7DB4 LD A,($7955)  ; (this load is overwritten)
 $7DB7 LD A,($7948)  ;
 $7DBA JR $7D89      ; AskWhich (HL = $7948 is pushed as the word)
